1019
01:36:24,174 --> 01:36:26,980
and then we are running the same evaluation results

1020
01:36:30,734 --> 01:36:32,484
against this new running of the task.

1021
01:36:32,752 --> 01:36:38,372
So we've changed the agent, we've rerun the agent, and we are rerunning the eval, and we're turning that into an experiment.

1022
01:36:39,278 --> 01:36:47,952
This is what the experiment looks like: experiments.run, we've given it a name, we've given it the data set that it should work on, we've given it the task,

1023
01:36:48,174 --> 01:36:50,692
we've given it the evaluator, and we've told it to run.

1024
01:36:53,870 --> 01:36:55,236
this gives us the results

1025
01:36:56,592 --> 01:36:57,872
which are here.

1026
01:37:00,366 --> 01:37:07,716
So for every single run, we've got the output that it got and the new eval score.

